# Line endings. The repository stores LF; without this file core.autocrlf smudged
# Windows checkouts to CRLF and those bytes reached the browser. Measured 2026-11-21
# on the merged main: a CRLF working copy changes the Vite content hashes
# (studio-Bz8EI3R_.js -> studio-B_D0mWBr.js, mount-next 375.93 kB -> 375.94 kB),
# rewrites the tracked web/studio.html, and tests/studio-page-drift.test.mjs already
# refuses a CRLF ui/studio.html for that same reason.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The PowerShell build scripts (scripts/build.ps1, scripts/build-android.ps1) stay in
# this rule: measured 2026-11-21 with `powershell.exe -NoProfile -File` on an LF-only
# script, which ran and parsed its blocks normally, so they need no CRLF exception.

# Byte-exact assets: no EOL logic may ever touch these.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.tflite binary
*.wasm binary
